<SizeGuide
  title="ASOS Size Guide — Is ASOS True to Size? (Charts & Tips) | Attirel"
  description="ASOS own-brand runs true to size with UK-first sizing. Full ASOS size charts with UK/US/EU conversions, plus how to handle the 850+ other brands ASOS stocks."
  brand="ASOS"
  verdictQuestion="Is ASOS true to size?"
  charts={charts}
>
  <Fragment slot="verdict">
    <strong>ASOS own-brand (ASOS DESIGN) is generally true to size</strong>, cut on a standard UK
    block. The catch: ASOS stocks hundreds of other brands, and each fits by its own chart —
    always check which brand you're actually buying. ASOS lists exact garment measurements on
    most product pages, which beats the generic chart every time.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="tips">
    <li><strong>ASOS sizes UK-first</strong> — US sizes are UK minus 4 for women (UK 12 = US 8); EU is UK plus 28 (UK 8 = EU 36).</li>
    <li><strong>Third-party brands:</strong> the size dropdown converts, but the fit block is the brand's own — a Nike M on ASOS fits like Nike, not like ASOS DESIGN.</li>
    <li><strong>Tall / Petite / Curve lines:</strong> same width sizing, different lengths and proportions — pick the line for your height first, then your usual size.</li>
    <li><strong>Use "View similar" garment measurements</strong> on the product page when available — pit-to-pit and length beat letter sizes.</li>
  </Fragment>
</SizeGuide>
